| phase-72 | `DONE` | B2-UI-2 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-72/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-UI-2 row). In-app locks no longer leave decrypted note content on the system clipboard: `ClipboardGuard` was only scrubbed on ON_PAUSE, and the in-app lock paths (manual "Lock Vault Now" `Dialogs.kt:673`, idle auto-lock `MainActivity.kt:255`, ON_STOP `:149`, ACTION_SCREEN_OFF `:122`) call `viewModel.lock()` directly — the app stays foregrounded so ON_PAUSE may never fire. Now `NoteflowViewModel.lock()` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:3218-3234`) calls `ClipboardGuard.scrubIfOwnCopy(appContext)` as its FIRST statement — before `repository.zeroizeKey()` and before the passwordless-vault gate, so every lock path + every vault kind scrubs. The decide → clear → forget logic is the new pure-JVM `services/ClipboardScrubPolicy.kt` (single decision table, `SCRUB_WINDOW_MS = 60_000`, `shouldScrub` refuses zero/expired timestamps) and `ClipboardGuard.scrubIfOwnCopy` now returns whether it cleared + forgets the copy timestamp after a scrub so a foreign (other-app) copy is NEVER wiped (a successful scrub leaves the next lock with nothing to clear). `clearPrimaryClipOverride` is an internal pure-JVM test seam; production still clears through the real system `ClipboardManager` (`clearPrimaryClip` API 28+ / empty `setPrimaryClip` API 26-27, best-effort so a platform failure never breaks the lock), and the ON_PAUSE scrub (`MainActivity.kt:145`) stays as defense-in-depth. Both note-content copy sources still stamp the guard before writing (`OcrResultDialog.kt:149-150`, `MediaEmbedComponents.kt:352-354`). No OS floor / fallback issue: `scrubIfOwnCopy` already handles API 26-27 (empty `setPrimaryClip`) vs API 28+ (`clearPrimaryClip`) and swallows any platform failure. Tests: new `B2Ui2ClipboardScrubTest` (13 — policy decision table incl. window boundary, recordCopy→scrub clears exactly once + forgets the timestamp, foreign/expired/no-app copies never wiped, failure-swallow, and source