| phase-82 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-06 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-82/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-06 row). Multi-layer PSD export no longer materializes N full-page ARGB bitmaps + N per-layer channel buffers at once — a ~25-layer note export dropped from ~350 MB peak heap to a bounded ~125-132 MB, on every export. New pure-JVM decision table `services/PsdExportPolicy.kt`: `MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT` = 16, `capLayerCount`/`omittedLayerCount`/`isLayerCountCapped` (the layer-budget arithmetic) + `noticeMessage` (the one-time non-alarming wording, says which end of the stack was kept). `ImportExportService.exportPageToPsd` (`:2422`) clamps before rendering: it keeps the TOP 16 DATA layers of `layers.sortedBy { it.zOrder }` (highest zOrder = the visually front-most, most recently worked-on layers) in bottom→top PSD record order via `takeLast(exportedDataLayers)`/`dropLast(exportedDataLayers)` (the old unbounded `sortedBy { it.zOrder }.forEachIndexed` bitmap-every-layer loop is gone; a restored crafted vault can no longer raise the bitmap count), folds the omitted BOTTOM layers into ONE bounded merged-preview bitmap (`compositeExtras`) so the PSD's flattened composite still shows the full page, and returns the new `PsdExportService.PsdExportOutcome(file, exportedLayerCount, omittedLayerCount)`; `EditorScreen.kt:1407-1420` shows "PSD export included the top N of M layers — K omitted (max 16)" via `PsdExportPolicy.noticeMessage` AFTER a successful export (a cancelled picker can no longer hide the omission behind "Export cancelled"; never silent degradation). `PsdExportService.exportLayersToPsd` now writes the layer-and-mask section STREAMING: the info records go into a tiny bounded buffer (`layerRecordBytes`, few KB for 16 layers), the per-layer channel PIXEL data is written straight to the destination `DataOutputStream` one channel at a time (`writeLayerChannelData` → `writeChannelPixels`) — the pre-fix `layerPixelBlocks` full-size per-layer channel `ByteArray` accumulation AND the per-layer `IntArray(width*height)` are gone — and ONE `IntArray(width*height)` is reused for every layer and the composite, with a defensive `take(MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT + 1)` clamp plus a bounded `compositeExtras.take(MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT)` composite pass. The section-length arithmetic (`channelSizeFor`/`channelDataLength`/`layerSectionLength`) keeps the PSD layout byte-identical to the pre-fix materialized section. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, API-26+ (pure JVM; the psd layout helpers are unit-testable without Android). Tests: new `B2Dos06PsdExportLayerCapTest` (16 — policy behavior incl. cap/clamp/omission/notice, the streaming writer's channel-size/section-length/layer-record byte layout, single-pixel-buffer reuse, hidden-layer flag, dedup + source pins: no `layerPixelBlocks`/`chanBos`, exactly one `IntArray(width * height)`, ImportExportService uses `PsdExportPolicy.capLayerCount` + `takeLast(exportedDataLayers)` + returns `PsdExportOutcome`, EditorScreen surfaces `PsdExportPolicy.noticeMessage`, merged-preview `compositeExtras` folding + `MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT + 1` defensive clamp pins). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1487 total green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-83 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-07 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-83/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-07 row). Backup export can no longer materialize the ENTIRE vault zip in heap and then make a second full-size AES-GCM copy (or a ~1.37x Base64 expansion) — a few-hundred-MB vault OOM'd the IO thread on every "Create backup", making the backup feature itself an interactive DoS. `ImportExportService.exportBackup` (`ImportExportService.kt:1268-1369`) now streams the archive INCREMENTALLY into a transient app-private staging file (`File(context.cacheDir, BackupExportPolicy.stagingFileName(backupName))` `:1279`; zip written entry-by-entry via `ZipOutputStream(FileOutputStream)` through `BackupExportPolicy.zipVaultEntriesToStream` `:1281` — the pre-fix `ByteArrayOutputStream` accumulation + `baos.toByteArray()` are gone), then the v2 password path encrypts FILE-TO-FILE through `BackupExportPolicy.encryptStreamGcm` (`:1338-1345`): header write, then a bounded 64 KiB `Cipher.update` chunk loop, then `doFinal` tail+tag — byte-identical to the pre-fix single `doFinal` by the JCE stream-mode contract (pinned by an assertArrayEquals vs the one-shot reference), so the on-disk `NFLB2` layout is unchanged and legacy restores (`decryptBackupPayload`) read it unmodified; the device-keyed path streams through `BackupExportPolicy.encryptStreamDeviceKeyedBase64` (`:1359-1363`): GCM chunked + `java.util.Base64.Encoder.wrap(NonClosingSink)` — the same legacy wire format (`[version][iv][ciphertext+tag]`), never the in-heap Base64 expansion. Peak heap is now one `ENCRYPT_CHUNK_BYTES` (64 KiB) buffer + one `Cipher.update` output + the tag, never the archive; the plaintext staging zip is app-private (cacheDir) and deleted in `finally` (`:1366`); the KEK is still zeroized (`:1347`). Single pure-JVM decision table `services/BackupExportPolicy.kt` (`ENCRYPT_CHUNK_BYTES` = 64 KiB, `STAGING_SUFFIX = ".zip-staging"`, `stagingFileName`, `IDLE_READ_LIMIT` guard vs a zero-progress stream, mirroring `AttachmentIngestPolicy`); `EncryptionService` GCM constants (`GCM_IV_LENGTH`/`GCM_TAG_LENGTH`/`PAYLOAD_VERSION`/`FIELD_AAD`) flipped `private`→`internal` only (same app module). Callers unchanged (HomeScreen device-keyed + password paths, WebDAV C2b, LocalSend VAULT_BACKUP — all consume the returned cacheDir `File`). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, API-26+ (pure `java.io` + `java.util.Base64`), no fallback required. Tests: new `B2Dos07BackupExportStreamingTest` (8 — streamed-v2 payload byte-identical to the one-shot reference AND decrypts via the real restore decryptor; streamed device-keyed backup round-trips via real `EncryptionService.decrypt`; chunk-budget invariants: a 6 MiB input is pulled in ~96 ≤64 KiB reads and written in ≤64 KiB+16-byte writes, never the archive; vault zip streams incrementally to the staging file and stays a valid zip with every entry byte-complete; 6.7 MiB synthetic-vault end-to-end: streamed export decrypts back to EXACTLY the staged archive and every zip entry matches; source pins: no `val zipData`/`baos.toByteArray()`/`fos.write(cipherText)`/`val encryptedBase64`/`encrypt(zipData` in exportBackup + staging/deletion policy wiring, exactly 2 `ByteArray(ENCRYPT_CHUNK_BYTES)` in the policy, no readBytes/toByteArray/ByteArrayOutputStream, Base64 wrap + FIELD_AAD + versioned wire format; staging name never becomes a public download name). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` green (full suite, 0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,773,954 bytes; one transient dex-merge OOM on the 2 GB default daemon retried clean with a 4 GB CLI heap — no `gradle.properties` change). |

| phase-84 | `DONE` | B2-CRYPTO-04 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-84/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-CRYPTO-04 row). Password-protected backups can no longer be created with a bare 6-char, no-complexity password, and the exported header no longer ships a cheap offline brute-force target. New pure-JVM policy `services/BackupPasswordPolicy.kt` (evaluate delegates to the single `PasswordStrengthPolicy` decision table used by the vault master password - >=8 NFKC-normalized graphemes, sequential/weak/low-diversity rejection, >=12-grapheme passphrase pass - plus `requireStrongBackupPassword` throwing `IllegalArgumentException` with verdict + `OFFLINE_BACKUP_NOTICE`). `ImportExportService.exportBackup` (`ImportExportService.kt:1346-1398`) replaces the old `normalizedGraphemeCount(backupPassword) >= MIN_PASSWORD_GRAPHEMES` bare-length require with `BackupPasswordPolicy.requireStrongBackupPassword(backupPassword)` and writes the new v3 `NFLB3` wire format: a fresh random 32-byte DEK-wrap key is split into [16B part1 (public header, `buildBackupHeaderV3` `:1173`)] + [16B part2 embedded at the start of the password-encrypted payload via `SequenceInputStream(ByteArrayInputStream(wrapKeyPart2), FileInputStream(stagingZip))` through `BackupExportPolicy.encryptStreamGcm` (`:1380-1390`)], so the public header alone holds HALF a key - an offline attacker can no longer test password guesses against a small wrapped-DEK blob; every crack attempt must fully decrypt the payload on top of PBKDF2. DEK wrap under `backup/dek-wrap` AAD, payload GCM under `backup/payload`+header AAD (B2-CRYPTO-03 domains), wrapKey + both halves + KEK all zeroized (`:1392-1397`). Restore/verify are format-agnostic over both magics (`parseBackupHeader` `:1540` reads `NFLB2`/`NFLB3`; `tryParseBackupV2`/`validateBackupPassword` now internal for tests) and NEVER strength-gate, so pre-fix weak-password backups still restore; v3 `validateBackupPassword` = ONE full payload decrypt + DEK unwrap (no cheap wrapped-DEK probe by design). The create-backup dialog (`HomeScreen.kt`) pre-checks `BackupPasswordPolicy.evaluate` and shows `OFFLINE_BACKUP_NOTICE` (restore dialog untouched). Also fixed a PRE-EXISTING latent zeroization-order bug the new tests exposed: `tryParseBackupV2` hex-encoded the unwrapped DEK AFTER `.fill(0)` (dekHex was all-zero - a password restore would rekey sqlcipher with a zero key); now hex-then-zeroize. Tests: new `B2Crypto04BackupPasswordTest` (11 - strength verdicts incl. old-accepted `123456`/`abcdef`/`A9fj2l!` now rejected, header carries only half the wrap key so the wrapped DEK cannot be opened from the header alone, wrong-password reject, v3 round-trip + v2 backward-compat, validate both magics never gates, export/parse/verify source pins); `B1Crypto04PasswordStrengthTest` whitelist updated for the sanctioned `BackupPasswordPolicy` reference. `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1506 total green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, pure-JVM/API-26 floor. |
| phase-85 | `DONE` | B1-NET-06 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-85/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-NET-06 status). LocalSend no longer probes the whole Wi-Fi /24 or broadcasts the device model without explicit user consent. Two-thirds predate this phase and are re-verified + pinned here: (1) `Build.MODEL` was already stripped from the announce/identity in phase-110 (B1-NET-09) — `services/localsend/LocalSendProtocol.kt:106-114` sends `alias = "InkFlow"`, `deviceModel = null`; this phase re-wires both to the NEW single pure-JVM decision table `services/localsend/LocalSendDiscoveryPolicy.kt` (`SENDER_ALIAS`, `senderDeviceModel = null`, `:43-46`) so the identity can never diverge from one source, and (2) opening the Send dialog was already silent — `discover()` (`LocalSendSendDialog.kt`) fires ONLY from the explicit "Find nearby devices"/"Refresh" `onClick` handlers, never a `LaunchedEffect`. The remaining live gap (the actual finding) was the /24 `legacyHttpScan` HTTP register sweep (`LocalSendSender.kt:197-218` walking `1..254`, `:232-258` POSTing `/api/localsend/v2/register`) that ran BY DEFAULT: `discoverDevices` had `includeLegacyHttpScan: Boolean = true` and the dialog hard-coded `= true` (`LocalSendSendDialog.kt:113`) — one tap on "Find nearby devices" gave every LAN host the app's presence + local IP via 254 register POSTs. Fix, all behind the new decision table: `discoverDevices` (`LocalSendSender.kt:104-118`) defaults `includeLegacyHttpScan` to `LEGACY_HTTP_SCAN_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT` (`false`) and the probe routes through `mayRunLegacyHttpScan(userOptedIn)` (fail closed; also only consulted when UDP discovery found nothing); the dialog seeds a "Also check every address on this Wi-Fi (slower; helps on networks that block discovery broadcasts)" Checkbox from that same `false` default and feeds the user's `legacyHttpScanOptIn` into the single discovery call — the sweep is now an explicit per-search user opt-in, a plain search emits ONLY a UDP announce/listen, and never a default silent subnet blast. Protocol stays pure-JVM/API-26; no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched; the only sender behavior change is on the LAN sweep path (`includeLegacyHttpScan=false` UDP-only search is the identical path to before-opt-in). Tests: new `B1Net06LocalSendDiscoveryGateTest` (7 — decision table: discovery requires explicit action + sweep off-by-default + fail-closed gate + identity wiring; source pins: sender default now reads the policy constant (never hard-coded `true`), dialog seeds opt-in from the policy and has no auto-discover effect, protocol identity wired to the policy constants, and a comment-stripped repo-wide scan proving no live `Build.MODEL` remains in `services/localsend/` main code — KDoc that merely documents the ban is handled, not a false positive). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1513 total green (0 failures, 0 skipped) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,779,638 bytes). |
| phase-86 | `DONE` | B1-NET-07 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-86/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-NET-07 status). The WebDAV remote-listing → download slice is now a pure-JVM decision table `services/WebDavRemoteListingPolicy.kt` (API-26 floor, no fallback needed): (1) `newestBackupHref` picks the href with the MAXIMUM filename timestamp across both name generations (`noteflow_vault_backup_<epochMillis>.nfb` legacy + `noteflow_vault_backup_<yyyy-MM-dd>_<token>.nfb` B2-CRYPTO-06) via `compareBy` ASCENDING + `maxWithOrNull` — a review-fix for the phase-86 initial commit's `compareByDescending`+`maxWithOrNull` inversion (which deterministically selected the OLDEST file, the exact rollback the finding is about) — unparseable names score lowest, same-timestamp ties break deterministically on the href, never XML document order (`WebDavSyncService.kt` `findBackupHrefs` + `newestBackupHref` replace `zipRegex`/`matches.last()` at `:290-297`); (2) the `.nfb` GET is streamed by `copyBounded` under `MAX_DOWNLOAD_BYTES` = 400 MB (mirrors the restore budget), checking the running total mid-loop so the target file never exceeds the cap, throwing the typed `DownloadTooLargeException` (whose message names the violation) and failing loudly on a contract-breaking zero-progress stream after `IDLE_READ_LIMIT` empty reads (`:337` wired; the too-large catch ALSO deletes the partial `webdav_download_import.nfb`); (3) `encodedRemoteFolderSegment` validates `remoteFolderName` as ONE path segment (blank/`.`/`..`/`/`/`\`/control chars rejected) and RFC 3986 percent-encodes it at all three URL interpolations (`:189/:226/:270`). Review-fix scoped the `copyTo` source pin to the download path only — the upload PUT keeps its genuinely-bounded local→server `input.copyTo(output)`. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Tests: `B1Net07WebDavDownloadPolicyTest` (19 — out-of-order hrefs pick the newest day-stamp, legacy epoch-millis newer-vs-day names, deterministic same-day tie-breaks, unparseable-name scoring, both name generations parsed/rejected, empty listing safely null, over-cap mid-stream abort without draining, exactly-at-cap accepted, byte-for-byte small copy, stalled-stream failure, folder segment round-trip/encode, traversal/control/blank rejection, download-path wiring pins). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1532 total — the only failure is the known pre-existing `WikiLinkParserCacheUnitTest` cancellation-timing flake (passes in isolation, documented in phases 67/70/74/76/79/80/81); `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,783,182 bytes, SHA-256 `0eecbb7e…`). |
| phase-87 | `DONE` | B1-DB-6 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-87/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-6 row). (1) WAL-aware tamper HMAC: the pre-fix main-file-only inline loop in `DatabaseSecurityHelper.computeDatabaseHmac` is replaced by the new pure-JVM `services/DatabaseHmacPolicy.kt` — `streamDbAndWal` streams `noteflow.sqlite` then its `-wal` companion through the same initialised `Mac`, so a WAL-only mutation committed between two checkpoints (the vault runs `JournalMode.WRITE_AHEAD_LOGGING`) is detected at the next verification; a cleanly-emptied WAL contributes byte-identical state to an absent WAL (no self-inflicted false positive), and every baseline-arming site already checkpoints first or reads a closed raw file (migration/export/restore stamps), so a freshly armed baseline covers `(main + empty/absent wal)`. (2) Per-session dismissal: `NoteflowViewModel.dismissDatabaseIntegrityWarning` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:1106-1109`) no longer writes `databaseIntegrityCheckEnabled = false` and neither dismissal path touches the persisted `databaseIntegrityWarningDismissed` latch (zero `settings.databaseIntegrityWarningDismissed` references remain in the VM); the banner routes through the new pure-JVM per-session `services/IntegrityWarningDismissalGate.kt` (`integrityWarningDismissal.mayShow()` in the init verify `:1091`, `.onDismiss(dontShowAgain)` `:1107`, `.onReenable()` `:1115` in `setDatabaseIntegrityCheckEnabled`), re-armed on every launch so the vault's only tamper tripwire can never be permanently killed by one tap; the checkbox is honestly relabelled "Don't show again this session" (`MainActivity.kt:362`). B1-CRYPTO-06's fail-open missing-checksum re-baseline at `verifyDatabaseIntegrity` `:147-152` is deliberately UNTOUCHED (its own phase-91 finding). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, API-26+ pure java.io/javax.crypto (no fallback needed). Tests: `B1Db06WalCoverageAndDismissalTest` (16 — WAL-frame mutation / appended-WAL / WAL-removal / main-mutation detection at the next verification, empty-WAL≡absent-WAL sameness, identical-state clean verify, per-session dismissal lifecycle incl. a two-session never-permanently-disabled model, source pins for the policy wiring + no persistent-flag reads/writes in the VM + the session-scoped checkbox label). |

| phase-88 | `DONE` | B1-DB-8 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-88/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-8 row). Decrypt-failure fallbacks never render RAW CIPHERTEXT as note content: every display-field decrypt site in `NoteRepository` routes through ONE pure-JVM decision table `services/DecryptFailurePolicy.kt` whose `render(storedValue, decrypted, isCiphertext)` is the ONLY render outcome allowed — legacy plaintext verbatim, authenticated ciphertext's plaintext, or `UNREADABLE_MARKER` ("Unreadable (decryption failed)"), never the raw base64 AES-GCM blob. The four pre-fix sinks are rewired: `getStrokesForPage` (`:946-960`) via `decryptFieldForDisplay`/`decryptStoredGeometryOrBlank` (unreadable geometry yields an EMPTY payload — no phantom ink, nothing fed to `deserializeStrokes`), `getMediaEmbedsForPage`, `getNoteVersions`, and `decryptPageIfNeeded` (the pre-fix catch-all that returned the page unchanged is gone). The structural classifier (`isStructuralCiphertext`) keeps legacy plaintext rows rendering verbatim — never "fixed" into the marker. Each failed auth while a DEK is actually present (a locked vault never inflates it) is recorded in a per-session deduped ledger (`NoteRepository.kt:79-99`) keyed per NOTE (`note:<pageId>`, phase-88 review fix — the initial field-level keying let one corrupted note's strokes/embeds cross the threshold on their own, so a one-note corruption can now never block the vault, and `decryptPageIfNeeded` no longer early-returns the raw page when the DEK is zeroized); once `PERSISTENT_FAILURE_THRESHOLD` = 10 DISTINCT records fail, `decryptFailureListener` fires once and `NoteflowViewModel.initializeDataCore` (`:1330-1343`) escalates to the existing corruption/restore event: `DatabaseSecurityHelper.setCorruptionDetected` + `_corruptionBlocked` (recovery screen: restore-from-backup / re-key / start-fresh) + a non-alarming `PERSISTENT_DECRYPT_FAILURE_NOTICE` snackbar — never silent degradation. The ledger + escalation are reset at every legitimate session boundary (`lock()`, re-key `changeMasterPassword`, WebDAV restore, and every `initializeData`). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Tests: `B1Db08DecryptFailureTest` (13 — real AES-GCM tampered/re-keyed/locked/legacy/authenticated reads + source pins for all four sinks and the VM escalation/reset wiring); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1561 total green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-89 | `DONE` | B1-PLAT-5 (LOW) **verify-only** (see `workspace/phase-89/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-PLAT-5 row). The finding was already closed by the phase-48 review fix: `PrivacyCrashReporter.sanitizeMessage` (`services/PrivacyCrashReporter.kt:85-96`) no longer uses the hardcoded-namespace regex (`/data/user/\d+/com\.authorss81\.noteflow/\S+`) that could never match the runtime data dir `/data/user/0/com.aistudio.inkflow.app.bkxjrz/`; it now redacts ANY app-private path structurally via `/data/user/\d+/\S+` (modern layout, any uid/package) + `/data/data/\S+` (legacy alias) → `[PATH_REDACTED]`. Pinned by `B2Log01CrashReportingTest` `:68-78` (namespace form) and `:80-90` (`crash entry redacts the real runtime applicationId data dir too` — asserts the exact `com.aistudio.inkflow.app.bkxjrz` string never appears). This phase made NO code change (PROMPT is SUPERSEDED; the hardcoded regex was not re-introduced) and re-verified: `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1561 tests green on re-run (the first run's single `WikiLinkParserCacheUnitTest` cancellation-timing flake passes in isolation — documented pre-existing flake since phase-67) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,786,602 bytes, SHA-256 `1a076fe6…`; a first assembleDebug invocation hit the documented unreproducible transient build failure, re-run green). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Out-of-scope (documented): `namespace`→applicationId alignment is B1-PLAT-6 / ROADMAP 21.10 (major architectural change, needs user approval). |
| phase-90 | `DONE` | B1-PLAT-8 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-90/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-PLAT-8 row). The NEW master-password floor is raised ≥ 10 NFKC-normalized graphemes and common/prefix-suffix words are rejected, with the "offline brute force is only mitigated by password entropy, never the on-device lockout" caveat documented in code + `docs/RELEASE.md`. `PasswordStrengthPolicy.MIN_STRENGTH_GRAPHEMES = 10` (`services/PasswordStrengthPolicy.kt:104`, was 8 after B1-CRYPTO-04 / 6 pre-fix B1-PLAT-8) + new `services/PasswordStrengthPolicy.kt` `isCommonPasswordVariant` (`:160`) / `PasswordStrengthVerdict.COMMON_PASSWORD` (`:64`) — a widely-leaked base word (`password`, `sunshine`, `letmein`, …) is refused whole or with only digit/symbol padding around it (`monkey5281`, `2026sunshine`, `letmein!!!`), structurally, so genuine passphrases that merely contain a word keep passing; sequential/repeated/class-diversity checks unchanged (`evaluate` `:141`, COMMON checked before LOW_DIVERSITY). **Phase-90 review fix (commit `llops: phase-90 review fixes`)**: `isCommonPasswordVariant` now runs FIRST in `evaluate` (after the 128 cap, before the 10 floor and before sequential), so bare `password`/`sunshine` and `password123`/`123password` report `COMMON_PASSWORD` — the review found the original build handed them a misleading `TOO_SHORT`/`SEQUENTIAL` verdict; accept/reject outcome is unchanged, only the reason string moved (pinned by new bare/sequential-pad assertions). Enforcement stays exactly at the set/rotate gate: `NoteflowViewModel.setMasterPassword` (`:2443`) + `changeMasterPassword` (`:2522`) route the NEW password through `PasswordStrengthPolicy.evaluate` (never at verify/unlock — pre-existing weaker vaults keep unlocking and rotating), the Dialogs.kt set/change dialogs surface `verdict.message`, and the backup gate `BackupPasswordPolicy` inherits the raised bar (a backup can never be protected by a password weaker than its vault). The exploit's premise (6-char + lockout gives false assurance) is closed on the CREATE side and documented on the OFFline side. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, pure JVM / API-26 floor (no fallback needed). Tests: `B1Crypto04PasswordStrengthTest` 17 green (3 new B1-PLAT-8 cases: bare/prefix-suffix common-word rejection, passphrase-tolerance, min=10 + RELEASE.md documentation pin); `B2Crypto04BackupPasswordTest` updated to the 10 floor (9-char now TOO_SHORT, `sunshine123` COMMON_PASSWORD, "10 characters" message) — `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1564 app tests green (0 failures, 0 skipped) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,787,778 B, SHA-256 `232ad7013ba0d8337c79b0366829fcccf37076d40d85bc4c523cadf6d41a7cbc`; the first invocation hit the documented transient dex-merge failure — retry green). |

| phase-91 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-06 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-91/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-06 row). The tamper baseline verification is FAIL-CLOSED and write-free. `DatabaseSecurityHelper.verifyDatabaseIntegrity` (`DatabaseSecurityHelper.kt:173-178`) now returns a sealed three-outcome `DatabaseIntegrityVerdict` from the single pure-JVM decision table `services/DatabaseIntegrityPolicy.kt` (API-26+ pure JVM, no fallback): `Verified` (stored baseline present + current main+`-wal` HMAC matches — compared via `ConstantTime.hexEqual`, B2-CRYPTO-01 full-length `MessageDigest.isEqual`), `Mismatch` (baseline present + differing bytes → genuine tamper), `CannotVerify` (baseline MISSING or current HMAC UN-COMPUTABLE → "cannot verify / possibly tampered"). Both pre-fix collapses are gone: the `stored==null → updateStoredChecksum(context); return true` silent re-baseline (an attacker deleting the `db_hmac_checksum` pref used to make the app bless a possibly-tampered file as "verified") and the `computeDatabaseHmac() ?: return true` trust-an-unverifiable-state. The function NEVER writes and NEVER re-baselines; `hasStoredChecksum` is the new read-only accessor and the pref stays write-only through `updateStoredChecksum`/`rearmBaselineFromFile` at the trusted arm sites (fresh-vault creation, migration, re-encrypt, backup, validate-then-arm restore). `NoteflowViewModel.verifyDatabaseIntegrityNow` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:1188-1193`) maps the verdict onto two distinct UI states: `Mismatch` keeps the existing per-session tamper banner (B1-DB-6 gate), `CannotVerify` surfaces a DISTINCT non-alarming notice (`MainActivity.kt` tertiaryContainer banner, wording from `DatabaseIntegrityPolicy.CANNOT_VERIFY_NOTICE` — vault NOT locked, NOT proven compromised, only unverified; shared per-session dismissal, honest "Don't show again this session" checkbox), `Verified` clears both. The ONLY auto-arm is a brand-new vault: `initializeDataCore` (`:1509-1520`) arms the baseline iff `!vaultFilePresentAtStart && !DatabaseSecurityHelper.hasStoredChecksum(appContext)` (a first-run vault false-alarming forever would be wrong, and there is no prior state to tamper) — an EXISTING vault whose baseline is missing/unreadable is never re-baselined from a live-file verify. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Tests: `B1Crypto06DatabaseIntegrityPolicyTest` (11 — decision table incl. both fail-closed sides, constant-time compare pin, write-free helper, read-only `hasStoredChecksum`, distinct VM state + verdict mapping incl. fresh-unarmed suppression, per-session dismissal reuse, MainActivity notice pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1577 total green (0 failures, 0 skipped) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,792,606 B, SHA-256 `8ecac53f…`). **Review fixes (commit `llops: phase-91 review fixes`)** (a) WAL-aware "fresh vault" probe (`vaultFilePresentAtStart` now counts a populated `-wal`, and `computeDatabaseHmac` stays computable for an empty main + populated WAL — a WAL-resident existing vault can never be silently re-baselined); (b) the first verification of a PASSWORDLESS vault is deferred past the initial data open (`firstDataInitDone` gate) so a mid-WAL-recovery hash can't false-Mismatch — locked vaults still verify at init; (c) `CannotVerify` honors the SAME per-session dismissal gate as `Mismatch`; (d) `MainActivity` banners deduplicated into one `IntegrityBannerCard` composable. No schema change, no new deps; `B1Crypto06DatabaseIntegrityPolicyTest` 14 green + `B1Db06` 16 green, `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1580 total green (0 failures). |
| phase-92 | `DONE` | B1-AUTH-07 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-92/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-AUTH-07 row). The create-backup dialog's pre-export master-password check (`NoteflowViewModel.isMasterPasswordValid`, sole caller `HomeScreen.kt:1316`) was a side-effect-free oracle — it ignored `lockoutActive()` and never bumped `failedUnlockAttempts`/`lockoutUntilEpochMs`, so an attacker with a brief window on an unlocked device could hammer the backup dialog with unlimited full-PBKDF2 guesses that never tripped the LockScreen's 5-attempt exponential lockout. BOTH master-password verification surfaces now share ONE persisted lockout. New `NoteflowViewModel.recordFailedMasterPasswordVerification()` (`:2867-2879`): bumps `_failedUnlockAttempts` + persisted `settings.failedUnlockAttempts`; at `MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS`=5 persists `settings.lockoutUntilEpochMs` via `computeLockoutDelayMs` (exponential backoff 30 s → 15 m cap, unchanged), starts the LockScreen countdown ticker, AND calls `lock()` so an in-app tripped lockout performs the same data-layer teardown as a real lock (B1-AUTH-02 posture — `dispose()` + no live keyed SQLCipher connection, `LockedOpenGuard` refuses fresh opens). New `resetMasterPasswordVerificationCounters()` (`:2886-2891`) zeroes `_failedUnlockAttempts` + both persisted counters + `_lockoutRemainingMs`. `verifyMasterPassword` (`:2806`) and `isMasterPasswordValid` (`:2917`/`:2921`) both delegate to the shared helpers — the old inline counter block in the verify catch (which read `settings.failedUnlockAttempts = newCount`) is GONE. `isMasterPasswordValid` now: `lockoutActive()` FIRST (refuses before any PBKDF2 work — the oracle is also closed under an active lockout), `masterPasswordCredentialOrLegacy == null` guard, failed attempt records via the shared helper, verified attempt still zeroizes the DEK (`dek.fill(0.toByte())`) then resets the counters. Deliberately still NO `PasswordStrengthPolicy` in `isMasterPasswordValid` (strength only gates set/rotate — weaker pre-existing vaults must keep unlocking; `B1Crypto04PasswordStrengthTest` asserts read). The backup dialog (`HomeScreen.kt:1316-1328`) still re-authenticates immediately before `ImportExportService.exportBackup(...)` (a tripped 5th attempt skips `checkpointWal`/`stampDatabaseChecksum`/`exportBackup` entirely) and now distinguishes a tripped/active lockout (`"Too many failed attempts. Try again after the lockout countdown."`) from a plain wrong password — never a silent degradation. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, pure JVM + existing Android call paths on the API 26+ floor (no fallback needed). Tests: `B1Auth07IsMasterPasswordOracleTest` (11 — behavioral `LockoutModel` with injectable clock: both surfaces share ONE counter set, 5th failure via either locks + persists 30 s backoff + data-layer lock, an active lockout refuses both surfaces BEFORE any PBKDF2 work and never churns counters, a correct password is still refused while locked, a verified attempt clears the shared counters, the lockout survives a restart and lapses past the backoff, exponential table 30 s→15 m cap, a credential-less vault refuses both surfaces without counting; source pins that `isMasterPasswordValid` enforces the lockout FIRST, routes through both helpers, zeroizes the DEK, stays strength-gate-free, and that `verifyMasterPassword`'s inline counter block is gone + HomeScreen verifies before `exportBackup` + surfaces the lockout message); `B1Crypto04PasswordStrengthTest` comment/message updated for the throttled-not-strength-gated verifier. `gradle testDebugUnitTest` **1591 total green** (0 failures, 0 skipped; the documented pre-existing `WikiLinkParserCacheUnitTest` cancellation-timing flake appeared in one earlier full-suite run and passes in isolation + did not reproduce on the final run) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,793,374 B, SHA-256 `881c83e3…`; first packageDebug invocation hit the documented transient incremental-packaging failure, retry green). **Phase-92 review fixes (commit `llops: phase-92 review fixes`)**: the two remaining inline success counter-resets — `verifyBiometricsAndUnlock` and `removeMasterPassword` — now delegate to the shared `resetMasterPasswordVerificationCounters()` so they cannot drift from the unlock/dialog path; `removeMasterPassword` additionally clears the stale `_lockoutRemainingMs` countdown its old inline block omitted (review FINDING #4). The `B1Auth07IsMasterPasswordOracleTest` `LockoutModel`'s backoff table is now source-pinned to production (`const val MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS = 5` + `computeLockoutDelayMs`'s `30_000L` seed / `(failures - MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS)` exponent / `exponent.coerceAtMost(5)` shift / `15 * 60 * 1000L` cap) so a model/production drift is caught (review FINDING #3). `workspace/phase-92/REPORT.md` now documents the unlock-path behavioral change from this phase: the pre-fix 5th UNLOCK failure only zeroized the key; post-fix a tripped threshold on ANY surface performs a full data-layer `lock()` (review FINDING #2 — deliberate B1-AUTH-02 strengthen, not a regression). Re-verified `gradle testDebugUnitTest` + `gradle assembleDebug` both green. |

| phase-93 | `DONE` | B2-LOG-04 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-93/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-LOG-04 row). No plugin failure text can echo an attacker-controllable `downloadUrl` into logcat and no CR/LF can forge a logcat line. New pure-JVM decision table `plugin-sdk/src/main/kotlin/com/authorss81/noteflow/plugins/PluginLogPolicy.kt` (phase-71's `FailureLogPolicy` pattern applied to the plugin pipeline): `hasLineBreak`/`lineBreakError`/`stripLineBreaks`/`safeLine` — `safeLine` strips CR/LF AND redacts `https?://\S+` tokens to `<url>`. The one production sink `AndroidPluginLogger` (`app/.../plugins/PluginLogger.kt:34-48`) routes BOTH `lifecycle` and `error` lines through `safeLine` (defense in depth). Parse-time rejection: `PluginEntry.validationErrors` (`plugin-sdk/.../runtime/PluginEntry.kt`) and `HostedPluginVersion.validationErrors` (`app/.../runtime/HostedPluginManifest.kt`) refuse CR/LF in `id`/`name`/`downloadUrl` via the fixed-text `lineBreakError` (the hostile value is never echoed), so a hostile manifest leg, a hand-edited catalog blob (`PluginEntryCodec.decode` → `isValid`) or a return-to-pinned update offer is refused whole (`PluginManifestParser.parse` → `Invalid`). Call sites log FIXED tokens only: `DownloadablePluginInstaller.failCleanup` (`:103-117`) logs `code=<reasonCode>` (`DOWNLOAD_GUARD`/`MISSING_SHA256`/`MISSING_CERT_PIN`/`VERIFY_FAILED`/`VERIFY_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`/`REGISTRY_REFUSED`/`LOAD_FAILED`/`LOAD_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`) and the download-refused early return logs `code=DOWNLOAD_GUARD` — the pre-fix `message.substringBefore('.')` line is GONE; `PluginStoreController` download/delete refusals (`:211`/`:241`) log `code=REGISTRY_REFUSED` (never `result.reason`); `DownloadablePluginUpdater` logs the fixed `post-update reload failed`; `PluginUpdateEngine.failedUpdateKeepsPrevious` (`:258-279`) logs `update failed; stage=<stageCode>` (`download`/`verification`/`load-smoke-test`/`swap-persist`) — the B2-LOG-04 exploit's URL-prefix leak through `reason.substringBefore('.')` (a transport failure `network failure https://attacker.example/exfil?…` used to print `network failure https://attacker`) is GONE. The downloader's own guard refusals were already log-free, now pinned by a test. `message`/`reason` remain user-facing (store dialog) only. Tests: new `B2Log04PluginLogScrubbingTest` (10 — policy table, model rejection, codec/manifest refusal, downloader quiet-guard, engine fixed-stage log). `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` 1602 total green (0 failures, 0 skipped) + `gradle testDebugUnitTest` (all modules) green + `gradle assembleDebug` green (first invocation hit the documented transient dex-merge failure; retry green, debug APK 173,794,594 B, SHA-256 `4219405b…`). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, API-26+ pure JVM. |

| phase-94 | `DONE` | B2-LOG-05 (LOW) fixed (see `workspace/phase-94/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-LOG-05 row). No WebDAV failure path can echo a raw exception message or a URL-derived string (and, via a `user:pass@` paste, the credentials) into the sync-status UI. New pure-JVM decision table `app/src/main/kotlin/com/authorss81/noteflow/services/WebDavFailurePolicy.kt` (phase-71 `FailureLogPolicy` pattern applied to UI text): fixed constants `CONNECT_FAILURE_MESSAGE`/`UPLOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGE`/`DOWNLOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGE`/`TOO_LARGE_DOWNLOAD_MESSAGE`/`INVALID_URL_MESSAGE`; `stripUrlUserInfo` (regex `([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*://)[^/@\s]*@` → drops the userinfo + its `@`); `scrubForDisplay` (userinfo strip AND `scheme://host/path` collapse to `host/...` via `URL_TOKEN_REGEX`); `configFailureText(e, fallback)` (scrubbed `e.message.orEmpty()`, blank → fallback); `refusalReason(e)` (FIXED tokens classifying resolver defusals — network-path / outside-configured-server / not-HTTPS / malformed-unusable / other — never the href or URL). `WebDavSyncService.kt`: the pre-fix `"Invalid WebDAV server URL: ${e.message}"` malformed-catch is now `throw IllegalArgumentException(WebDavFailurePolicy.INVALID_URL_MESSAGE)` (the JVM `MalformedURLException` message dumps the user's RAW input — a `https://user:pass@…` paste exported its credentials through the exception text); `validateServerUrl` returns the userinfo-stripped normalized URL; `testAndPrepareConnection` → IllegalArgument = `configFailureText(e, INVALID_URL_MESSAGE)`, blanket = `CONNECT_FAILURE_MESSAGE` (was `"Connection failed: ${e.localizedMessage ?: e.message}"`); `uploadEncryptedVault` → IllegalArgument = `configFailureText(...)`, blanket = `UPLOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGE`; `downloadLatestEncryptedVault` → resolver IllegalArgument = `"Sync refused: ${refusalReason(e)}"`, origin-gate IllegalState = FIXED "Sync refused: ... configured WebDAV server." (dropped `${e.message}`), too-large = `TOO_LARGE_DOWNLOAD_MESSAGE` (was `e.message ?: "Remote backup archive is too large..."`), blanket = `DOWNLOAD_FAILURE_MESSAGE`. `WebDavSyncDialog.kt` scrubs all three status renders (upload `res.message`, restore `failureMessage`, download `res.message`) through `WebDavFailurePolicy.scrubForDisplay(...)` — defense in depth so even a future sink can't render raw text. Grep-pinned in the test: zero `localizedMessage`, zero `${e.message}`, zero bare `res.message`-assign in both production files; exactly 2 code reads of `e.message` (`configFailureText` + `refusalReason`), both only through `scrubForDisplay`. Auth/HTTP-status branches were already fixed strings and are left untouched. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, API-26+ pure JVM. Tests: new `B2Log05WebDavFailureTextTest` (13 — userinfo stripping incl. the http-opt-in local URL, userinfo-free URLs unchanged, malformed-URL fixed message carrying NO secret echo, fixed constants never interpolate (`"\${"` absent) and none of the five category strings appears in the service, connect failure whose exception embeds credentials yields the fixed constant with scrubbed text free of secrets, scrubForDisplay/stripUrlUserInfo behavior, refusalReason token classification, configFailureText fallback, plus source pins on `WebDavSyncService.kt`/`WebDavSyncDialog.kt`/`WebDavFailurePolicy.kt`). `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` (WebDAV families incl. existing `WebDavSyncServiceTest`/`WebDavHrefResolverTest`/`B1Net07WebDavDownloadPolicyTest`) green, then `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1619 total green (0 failures, 0 skipped) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
